.TH WGESTURES 1 "August 2026" "WGestures 2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wgestures \- control and configure global mouse gestures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wgestures
[\fB\-\-settings\fR | \fB\-\-enable\fR | \fB\-\-disable\fR |
 \fB\-\-pause\fR | \fB\-\-resume\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR |
 \fB\-\-diagnose\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
WGestures uses a GNOME Shell 46 extension in GNOME Wayland sessions and a
Python/GTK3 daemon in X11 sessions. Configuration is stored below
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wgestures\fR.
The X11 daemon starts from the desktop autostart entry and exposes a tray menu.
GNOME Shell uses its native top-panel indicator. Successful gestures briefly
show their action name near the pointer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the desktop-appropriate preferences application.
.TP
.BR \-\-enable ", " \-\-disable
Enable or disable gesture capture for the current user.
.TP
.BR \-\-pause ", " \-\-resume
Temporarily pause or resume gesture capture.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the selected backend and current capture state.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Inspect the distribution, graphical session, dependencies, configuration,
XTEST availability and runtime grab status.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable diagnostic output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wgestures/gestures-v1.json
Gesture and action configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/wgestures-autostart.desktop
X11 session startup entry.
.SH SECURITY
Command actions execute through \fI/bin/sh -lc\fR with the current user's
permissions. Only configure commands from trusted sources. Legacy .wg2 files
are parsed with an allow-list and their $type metadata is never instantiated.
